["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>Know what is inside the bird and you know where to shoot, how to keep the meat, and why grouse act the way they do.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Side view cutaway of a grouse facing right. The crop sits at the base of the neck. The heart sits low and forward in the chest. The lungs sit high against the back. Air sacs fill much of the body behind the lungs. The gizzard sits in the middle of the belly, and the two long ceca run toward the tail. The big breast muscle sits along the keel bone underneath.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Inside a grouse</text>\n<path d=\"M60 150 Q70 90 150 85 Q230 80 270 100 Q300 70 330 72 Q356 74 360 96 L382 104 L360 110 Q352 130 320 140 Q300 200 230 215 Q140 230 90 205 L20 210 L30 185 L10 170 L60 160 Z\" fill=\"#efe3cf\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n<circle cx=\"340\" cy=\"92\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#23261f\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"200\" cy=\"200\" rx=\"95\" ry=\"18\" fill=\"#f2d7c9\" stroke=\"#c9a491\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<path d=\"M125 214 Q200 236 285 210\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"4\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"240\" cy=\"112\" rx=\"32\" ry=\"12\" fill=\"#b5524a\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"262\" cy=\"160\" rx=\"13\" ry=\"16\" fill=\"#c23b22\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"300\" cy=\"132\" rx=\"16\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#e9c46a\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"175\" cy=\"125\" rx=\"40\" ry=\"20\" fill=\"#cfe0ef\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"200\" cy=\"172\" rx=\"18\" ry=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/>\n<path d=\"M150 170 Q110 160 90 175 Q110 186 150 178\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#7d6b3a\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n<line x1=\"300\" y1=\"132\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"161\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n<text x=\"330\" y=\"175\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Crop</text>\n<line x1=\"262\" y1=\"160\" x2=\"290\" y2=\"241\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n<text x=\"290\" y=\"255\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Heart</text>\n<line x1=\"240\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"260\" y2=\"62\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n<text x=\"260\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Lungs</text>\n<line x1=\"175\" y1=\"125\" x2=\"140\" y2=\"62\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n<text x=\"140\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Air sacs</text>\n<line x1=\"200\" y1=\"172\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"241\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"255\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Gizzard</text>\n<line x1=\"100\" y1=\"172\" x2=\"50\" y2=\"241\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n<text x=\"50\" y=\"255\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Ceca</text>\n<line x1=\"130\" y1=\"205\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"266\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n<text x=\"100\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Breast on the keel</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Big white breast for bursts; crop, gizzard and ceca for tough food (75 to 85%).</li><li>Lungs high on the back, heart low and forward <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the body in one list</summary><ul><li>Crop: a stretchy pouch at the base of the neck that holds a meal <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Gizzard: a muscular stomach that grinds food with swallowed grit <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Ceca: two long blind pouches where bacteria break down woody fibre <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Lungs: small and rigid, tucked against the ribs and backbone <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Air sacs: thin balloons that move air through the lungs; they also reach into some bones (70 to 80%).</li><li>Heart: four chambers, low and forward in the chest <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Breast: two big flight muscles on the keel bone, white meat <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Front view slice through a grouse. The backbone is at the top with the lungs on each side of it. Below, the two big breast muscles hang on each side of the keel, the blade shaped breastbone. Breast muscle is white meat built for short bursts of power.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Front view slice: the meat</text>\n<path d=\"M200 70 Q300 75 320 150 Q320 230 200 268 Q80 230 80 150 Q100 75 200 70 Z\" fill=\"#efe3cf\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n<path d=\"M200 140 Q290 140 300 180 Q290 240 200 262 Z\" fill=\"#f2d7c9\" stroke=\"#c9a491\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<path d=\"M200 140 Q110 140 100 180 Q110 240 200 262 Z\" fill=\"#f2d7c9\" stroke=\"#c9a491\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<polygon points=\"196,140 204,140 206,272 194,272\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"90\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"160\" cy=\"112\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"12\" fill=\"#b5524a\"/><ellipse cx=\"240\" cy=\"112\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"12\" fill=\"#b5524a\"/>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Backbone</text>\n<line x1=\"80\" y1=\"64\" x2=\"188\" y2=\"88\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n<text x=\"320\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Lungs</text>\n<line x1=\"330\" y1=\"64\" x2=\"258\" y2=\"108\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n<text x=\"318\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Breast:</text>\n<text x=\"318\" y=\"218\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">white meat,</text>\n<text x=\"318\" y=\"236\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">burst power</text>\n<line x1=\"316\" y1=\"196\" x2=\"290\" y2=\"196\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n<text x=\"6\" y=\"214\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Keel: the</text>\n<text x=\"6\" y=\"232\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">breastbone</text>\n<text x=\"6\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">blade</text>\n<line x1=\"80\" y1=\"228\" x2=\"194\" y2=\"250\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>The keel is a blade on the breastbone that anchors the flight muscles <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>White breast: power for a few seconds. Dark legs: walking all day <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: why white and dark meat</summary><ul><li>Grouse breast meat is white: fast muscle fibres with little myoglobin that run on stored sugar and tire fast (70%, studies on turkeys and chickens, close cousins).</li><li>That is why a grouse explodes up, flaps hard, then glides: the breast cannot keep flapping long <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>. Pennsylvania notes the glide is usually under 90 m (100 yd) <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Leg and thigh meat is darker: slow muscle that works all day as the bird walks <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>. Grouse walk more than they fly (75%, Pennsylvania Game Commission).</li><li>Bird bones are light; some are hollow and filled with air sac extensions <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Meat note: the breast is most of the meat on a grouse. The leg is small but tasty (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 290\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation of a grouse breathing. Step 1: on the in breath, fresh air flows down the windpipe past the lung into the rear air sacs. Step 2: the bird squeezes, and the rear sacs push the air one way through the rigid lung, where oxygen goes into the blood. Step 3: on the next breath the used air moves to the front sacs and out. Fresh air crosses the lung in one direction.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"290\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">How a grouse breathes</text>\n<path d=\"M50 170 Q60 110 160 105 Q250 100 300 120 L340 100 L370 110 L340 130 Q320 220 200 235 Q90 235 50 170 Z\" fill=\"#efe3cf\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"120\" cy=\"175\" rx=\"48\" ry=\"30\" fill=\"#cfe0ef\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"290\" cy=\"170\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"22\" fill=\"#cfe0ef\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<rect x=\"185\" y=\"118\" width=\"70\" height=\"24\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#b5524a\"/>\n<text x=\"220\" y=\"135\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Lung</text>\n<text x=\"120\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Rear sacs</text>\n<text x=\"290\" y=\"176\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Front</text>\n<path d=\"M370 108 L330 112 L290 150\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"5\"/>\n<path id=\"mgr-air-sacs-p1\" d=\"M370 108 L330 112 L280 130 L200 150 L130 172\" fill=\"none\"/>\n<path id=\"mgr-air-sacs-p2\" d=\"M130 172 L190 132 L250 130 L290 168\" fill=\"none\"/>\n<path id=\"mgr-air-sacs-p3\" d=\"M290 168 L300 140 L330 112 L380 104\" fill=\"none\"/>\n<circle r=\"6\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"0s\"/><animateMotion dur=\"2.5s\" begin=\"0s\" fill=\"freeze\"><mpath href=\"#mgr-air-sacs-p1\"/></animateMotion><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"3.2s\"/></circle>\n<circle r=\"6\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"3.2s\"/><animateMotion dur=\"2.5s\" begin=\"3.2s\" fill=\"freeze\"><mpath href=\"#mgr-air-sacs-p2\"/></animateMotion><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"6.4s\"/></circle>\n<circle r=\"6\" fill=\"#9aa0a6\" opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"6.4s\"/><animateMotion dur=\"2s\" begin=\"6.4s\" fill=\"freeze\"><mpath href=\"#mgr-air-sacs-p3\"/></animateMotion><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"8.8s\"/></circle>\n<circle r=\"6\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"0.25s\"/><animateMotion dur=\"2.5s\" begin=\"0.25s\" fill=\"freeze\"><mpath href=\"#mgr-air-sacs-p1\"/></animateMotion><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"3.2s\"/></circle>\n<circle r=\"6\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"3.45s\"/><animateMotion dur=\"2.5s\" begin=\"3.45s\" fill=\"freeze\"><mpath href=\"#mgr-air-sacs-p2\"/></animateMotion><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"6.4s\"/></circle>\n<circle r=\"6\" fill=\"#9aa0a6\" opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"6.65s\"/><animateMotion dur=\"2s\" begin=\"6.65s\" fill=\"freeze\"><mpath href=\"#mgr-air-sacs-p3\"/></animateMotion><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"8.8s\"/></circle>\n<circle r=\"6\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"0.5s\"/><animateMotion dur=\"2.5s\" begin=\"0.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"><mpath href=\"#mgr-air-sacs-p1\"/></animateMotion><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"3.2s\"/></circle>\n<circle r=\"6\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"3.7s\"/><animateMotion dur=\"2.5s\" begin=\"3.7s\" fill=\"freeze\"><mpath href=\"#mgr-air-sacs-p2\"/></animateMotion><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"6.4s\"/></circle>\n<circle r=\"6\" fill=\"#9aa0a6\" opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"6.9s\"/><animateMotion dur=\"2s\" begin=\"6.9s\" fill=\"freeze\"><mpath href=\"#mgr-air-sacs-p3\"/></animateMotion><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"8.8s\"/></circle>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"0s\"/><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"3.2s\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">1. Breathe in: fresh air goes past the lung to the rear sacs</text></g>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"3.2s\"/><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"6.4s\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">2. Squeeze: the sacs push it one way through the lung</text></g>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"6.4s\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">3. Next breath: used air leaves by the front sacs</text></g>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"8.8s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><rect x=\"40\" y=\"52\" width=\"320\" height=\"30\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"73\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Fresh air crosses the lung one way</text></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Fresh air crosses the lung one way. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Rigid lungs, air sacs as bellows <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Air flows one way through the lung, in breath and out <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the air sac system in plain words</summary><ul><li>A bird's lungs do not swell like ours. The air sacs expand and squeeze to push air through them (80%, 2024 review in a peer reviewed journal; biology textbook).</li><li>Most birds have about 9 air sacs, in a front set and a rear set <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>On the in breath much of the fresh air goes past the lung into the rear sacs. On the out breath that air is pushed through the lung. Gas exchange happens only in the lung, not in the sacs <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>No diaphragm: the ribs and keel move to pump the sacs <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Result: fresh air crosses the lung on both in and out breaths. Birds get more oxygen per breath than we do <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Hunting meaning: a pellet through the lungs or the big sacs takes the bird's breath; a hit only in the back half often does not stop it fast (Tip, 60%).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 290\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Side view of a grouse. The heart sits low and forward in the chest, under the front of the breast meat and behind the wing root. The lungs sit above it, against the back. The head and neck sit just in front, circled as the target zone for a .22 so the breast meat is saved.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"290\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Where the vitals sit</text>\n<g transform=\"translate(200 170) scale(3.2 3.2)\"><polygon points=\"-20,-6 -38,-20 -48,-12 -52,0 -48,8 -20,8\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M-40 -18 Q-50 -10 -48 6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"15\" fill=\"#c9a77f\"/><circle cx=\"21\" cy=\"-14\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#c9a77f\"/><polygon points=\"16,-20 20,-28 25,-20\" fill=\"#c9a77f\"/><polygon points=\"28,-16 35,-13 28,-10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><circle cx=\"23\" cy=\"-16\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><path d=\"M2 13 l-2 11 M10 13 l2 11\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\"/></g>\n<ellipse cx=\"214\" cy=\"146\" rx=\"32\" ry=\"11\" fill=\"#b5524a\" opacity=\".9\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"250\" cy=\"182\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"18\" fill=\"#c23b22\" opacity=\".9\"/>\n<circle cx=\"267\" cy=\"124\" r=\"34\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\"/>\n<text x=\"320\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Head and</text>\n<text x=\"320\" y=\"88\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">neck</text>\n<line x1=\"310\" y1=\"94\" x2=\"285\" y2=\"108\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"80\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Lungs</text>\n<line x1=\"96\" y1=\"84\" x2=\"205\" y2=\"142\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n<text x=\"110\" y=\"268\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Heart: low, forward</text>\n<line x1=\"160\" y1=\"255\" x2=\"244\" y2=\"192\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n<text x=\"395\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">Behind the wing root,</text>\n<text x=\"395\" y=\"268\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">under the front breast</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Four chambered heart, big for the body <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Brain, spine, heart and lungs are all in the front half <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what it means for the shot</summary><ul><li>Bird hearts have two atria and two ventricles, with the two sides fully separate, like ours. The main artery curves right, not left (80%, avian heart review).</li><li>Birds carry relatively large hearts for flight <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Body temperature runs hot: about 41.5 C in captive ruffed grouse, range 40.4 to 42.6 C <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>.22: the head or upper neck kills cleanly and saves the breast (Tip, 70%). See <a href=\"#/s/mc-grouse-09/3\">How to hunt</a>.</li><li>Shotgun: put the pattern on the head and front half. Pellets in the head, neck and chest stop the bird (Tip, 70%).</li><li>A grouse hit only in the wing or rear may run and hide. Mark it and go fast (Tip). See <a href=\"#/s/mc-grouse-10\">Shot to table</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Flow chart of a grouse gut. Bill: picks buds and berries. Crop: stores a meal at the base of the neck. Gizzard: grinds food with swallowed grit. Intestine: absorbs. Ceca: two long pouches that ferment fibre. In winter the ceca and gut grow longer for woody food. Open the crop of a bird you shoot to see what they eat.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">The food path</text>\n<rect x=\"12\" y=\"50\" width=\"116\" height=\"76\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"70\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Bill</text>\n<text x=\"70\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">picks buds, berries</text>\n<rect x=\"140\" y=\"50\" width=\"116\" height=\"76\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fbe3d3\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"198\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Crop</text>\n<text x=\"198\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">stores a meal</text>\n<rect x=\"268\" y=\"50\" width=\"116\" height=\"76\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fbe3d3\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"326\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Gizzard</text>\n<text x=\"326\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">grinds with grit</text>\n<rect x=\"12\" y=\"160\" width=\"116\" height=\"76\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"70\" y=\"190\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Intestine</text>\n<text x=\"70\" y=\"214\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">absorbs</text>\n<rect x=\"140\" y=\"160\" width=\"116\" height=\"76\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fbe3d3\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"198\" y=\"190\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Ceca</text>\n<text x=\"198\" y=\"214\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">ferment fibre</text>\n<line x1=\"128\" y1=\"88\" x2=\"140.0\" y2=\"88.0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><polygon points=\"140.0,88.0 131.0,92.3 131.0,83.7\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<line x1=\"256\" y1=\"88\" x2=\"268.0\" y2=\"88.0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><polygon points=\"268.0,88.0 259.0,92.3 259.0,83.7\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<line x1=\"326\" y1=\"126\" x2=\"326.0\" y2=\"140.0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><polygon points=\"326.0,140.0 321.7,131.0 330.3,131.0\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<path d=\"M326 126 Q326 150 200 150 Q70 150 70 160\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n<line x1=\"70\" y1=\"152\" x2=\"70.0\" y2=\"160.0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><polygon points=\"70.0,160.0 65.7,151.0 74.3,151.0\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<line x1=\"128\" y1=\"198\" x2=\"140.0\" y2=\"198.0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><polygon points=\"140.0,198.0 131.0,202.3 131.0,193.7\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<text x=\"270\" y=\"190\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Winter: ceca and</text>\n<text x=\"270\" y=\"208\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">gut grow longer</text>\n<text x=\"270\" y=\"226\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">for woody food</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"285\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Pull the crop open after the shot: it shows what they eat.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Crop stores, gizzard grinds, ceca ferment <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Open the crop of every bird you shoot: it shows the food (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: digestion step by step</summary><ul><li>A grouse can fill its crop with a day's worth of buds in about 20 minutes, then sit somewhere safe to digest (60%, Northern Woodlands).</li><li>The gizzard uses swallowed grit to grind seeds, buds and needles <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>. That is why grouse pick gravel on road edges and dust bowls <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>The ceca hold bacteria that ferment fibre from woody food like aspen and birch buds <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Ruffed grouse prefer aspen flower buds and avoid birch and alder catkins when they can choose (80%, Guglielmo and Karasov 1995).</li><li>Field use: slit the crop and look. Clover leaves, kinnikinnick berries, aspen buds or pine needles tell you exactly where to hunt next (Tip, common hunter practice).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 290\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bar chart for spruce grouse. Gut length in winter is about 40 percent longer than in summer. In the snow season, conifer needles make up 99 percent of the diet. Alberta study by Pendergast and Boag, 1973, 75 percent.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"290\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Summer gut vs winter gut (spruce grouse)</text>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Gut length</text>\n<rect x=\"20\" y=\"80\" width=\"200\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<text x=\"228\" y=\"99\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">summer</text>\n<rect x=\"20\" y=\"112\" width=\"280\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<text x=\"308\" y=\"131\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">winter, +40%</text>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"175\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Snow season diet</text>\n<rect x=\"20\" y=\"185\" width=\"360\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<rect x=\"20\" y=\"185\" width=\"356\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"204\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Conifer needles: 99%</text>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"248\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Alberta study, Pendergast and Boag 1973 (75%).</text>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">A longer gut gets more from tough needles.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>In winter the gut grows longer to handle needles and buds <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Spruce grouse: 99% needles once snow covers the ground <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: numbers</summary><ul><li>Alberta spruce grouse: conifer needles were 79% of the year's diet by dry weight and 99% during the snow season (75%, Pendergast and Boag 1973, via summaries).</li><li>Gut sections grow about 40% longer in winter <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>. One secondary source says the gizzard grows about 75% (60%, <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>).</li><li>Ceca enlarge in winter when only needles are eaten <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Taste: late season spruce grouse living on needles can taste of pine; soak or brine (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 290\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Cross section of a snow roost. A grouse dives from the air into soft snow, tunnels a short way and sits in a small chamber under 20 centimetres or more of snow. Outside air can be as cold as minus 35 degrees Celsius, while the roost stays between minus 3 and minus 12, 75 percent.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"290\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">A snow roost: a grouse igloo</text>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"230\" width=\"400\" height=\"60\" fill=\"#c9b79c\"/>\n<path d=\"M0 120 Q200 110 400 122 L400 230 L0 230 Z\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#b9c6d3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<path d=\"M70 118 Q90 150 150 175 Q200 190 240 185\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#b9c6d3\" stroke-width=\"18\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"262\" cy=\"182\" rx=\"40\" ry=\"24\" fill=\"#e8eef4\" stroke=\"#b9c6d3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(262 184) scale(0.75 0.75)\"><polygon points=\"-20,-6 -38,-20 -48,-12 -52,0 -48,8 -20,8\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><path d=\"M-40 -18 Q-50 -10 -48 6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"15\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><circle cx=\"21\" cy=\"-14\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><polygon points=\"16,-20 20,-28 25,-20\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><polygon points=\"28,-16 35,-13 28,-10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><circle cx=\"23\" cy=\"-16\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><path d=\"M2 13 l-2 11 M10 13 l2 11\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\"/></g>\n<text x=\"70\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Air: as cold as -35 C</text>\n<text x=\"220\" y=\"252\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Inside: -3 to -12 C (75%)</text>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Dives in from the air</text>\n<line x1=\"370\" y1=\"124\" x2=\"370\" y2=\"230\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"362\" y=\"160\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"bold\">20 cm+</text>\n<text x=\"362\" y=\"178\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">soft snow</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Grouse run about 41.5 C inside <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Soft snow 20 cm deep turns into a shelter <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: winter survival tools</summary><ul><li>Snow roost: under 20 cm of soft snow, roost temperatures stayed between -3 and -12 C while the air dropped as low as -35 C (75%, Wilson Bulletin).</li><li>In Maine, grouse plunged into the snow in flight once it was about 40 cm deep <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>. A study found grouse stress hormones fall sharply once snow is deeper than 20 cm <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Snow roosts can be 11 to 17 C (20 to 30 F) warmer than open air (75%, Idaho Fish and Game).</li><li>Snowshoes: in winter grouse grow comb like scales on the sides of their toes, called pectinations (85%, Hinterland Who's Who).</li><li>Ptarmigan grow feathered feet, unique among chicken like birds <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>No good snow? A crust or bare cold ground forces grouse into thick conifers; they lose weight and some starve or freeze (85%, Hinterland Who's Who).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 290\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Dot chart of 100 ruffed grouse chicks: about 24 survive, the rest die in the first 5 weeks, most in the first week. Pennsylvania Game Commission figures, 75 percent. Adults: about 1 in 2 lives through a year, few reach age 2, and January to March are the hardest months.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"290\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">100 ruffed grouse chicks</text>\n<circle cx=\"30\" cy=\"52\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"47\" cy=\"52\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"64\" cy=\"52\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"81\" cy=\"52\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"98\" cy=\"52\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"115\" cy=\"52\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"132\" cy=\"52\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"149\" cy=\"52\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"166\" cy=\"52\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"183\" cy=\"52\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"52\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"217\" cy=\"52\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"234\" cy=\"52\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"251\" cy=\"52\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"268\" cy=\"52\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"285\" cy=\"52\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"302\" cy=\"52\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"319\" cy=\"52\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"336\" cy=\"52\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"353\" cy=\"52\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"30\" cy=\"69\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"47\" cy=\"69\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"64\" cy=\"69\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"81\" cy=\"69\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"98\" cy=\"69\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"115\" cy=\"69\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"132\" cy=\"69\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"149\" cy=\"69\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"166\" cy=\"69\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"183\" cy=\"69\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"69\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"217\" cy=\"69\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"234\" cy=\"69\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"251\" cy=\"69\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"268\" cy=\"69\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"285\" cy=\"69\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"302\" cy=\"69\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"319\" cy=\"69\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"336\" cy=\"69\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"353\" cy=\"69\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"30\" cy=\"86\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"47\" cy=\"86\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"64\" cy=\"86\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"81\" cy=\"86\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"98\" cy=\"86\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"115\" cy=\"86\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"132\" cy=\"86\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"149\" cy=\"86\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"166\" cy=\"86\" r=\"6.5\" fill